# experiment-1 output tree — commit results + the run record; drop the cache.
# The root .gitignore ignores `logs/`, `*.log`, `*.out` globally; the negations
# below re-include the operational logs. Patterns are relative to experiment-1/.
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments — keep every comment on its own line.

# 31 GB regeneratable cache (embeddings.npy, chunks.json, parsed corpus).
# This is ~all of the tree's weight; everything else is small result artifacts.
.shared_cache/

# Transient scheduler markers (no value post-run).
.scheduler_*

# ── Operational logs: re-include what the root .gitignore would drop ──
# Let git descend into logs/ (overrides the root `logs/` rule):
!logs/
# Re-ignore its contents by default, then keep the specific files below:
logs/*
# scheduler.log + the 79 per-unit stdout logs (~21 MB):
!logs/*.log
# final status snapshot:
!logs/STATUS.json
# logs/nohup.out and logs/scheduler.pid stay ignored by the `logs/*` line above.

# Per-seed run.log under the method dirs stays ignored by the root `*.log`
# rule (~150 MB verbose framework logs) — intentionally nothing here.

# Optuna study internals — binary, resume-only, redundant with the readable
# history.jsonl / search_result.json. The run is done; we never resume a study.
optuna.db
*.pkl
